<h1 class="page-title">Yichi(Dios) Yang</h1>
<div class="about-copy">
  <p>Hi, I’m a Machine Learning Engineer and Data Scientist with a strong passion for interpreting the world through data—and let data speak back in insight. I completed a Bachelor degree in joint of mathematics and economics in New York University and earned a Master of Arts in Statistics from Columbia University.</p>
  <p>I hold a solid background in statistics, programming, and applied mathematics, and have worked on projects spanning large-scale data processing, model interpretability, and end-to-end machine learning pipelines—from data exploration and feature engineering to deployment. More importantly, I believe that feature selection is not merely a step for improving performance—it’s a window into the deeper structure of the data. I’m driven by the pursuit of understanding how variables connect, interact, and ultimately shape outcomes. To me, machine learning is not just about prediction—it’s about uncovering the logic of the world through data.</p>
  <p>Just as I seek structure and meaning in data, I find joy in capturing the subtle patterns of everyday life through photography. Whether it’s the play of light and shadow, the rhythm of a crowded street, or a fleeting moment of stillness—I enjoy observing the world’s hidden logic through a different lens. Photography, for me, is another way of learning to see.</p>
</div>
